# Build trees. build.zig writes everything under build/<target>; the suffixed names below
# belonged to the CMake and docker lanes and are kept only so a tree left behind by a
# pre-C22 checkout does not show up in `git status`.
build
install
build*32
build*64
build_deb*
build_ubuntu*
build_win*
build_doc
build_native
install_native
install*32
install*64
Debug
debug
gcc
clang
ssc_debian
ssc_windows
.zig-cache/
*.o

# The libc++ dependency closures built by tools/deps/, and the upstream sources they share
# (libcxx-src/). Multi-GB: the recipes are committed, the result is not. Deliberately not under
# build/ -- a clean must not discard a build measured in hours.
#
# No trailing slash: a closure shared between clones is reached by a symlink, and git matches
# a symlink as a file however directory-like it looks.
/libcxx-*

# Test droppings: run_all_tests and the tutorials write these into their cwd,
# which is the repo root.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED ON PURPOSE. Bare **.png / **.pptx / **.h5 also match the tracked
# reference datasets under validation/ and integration_tests/. Git keeps those because
# they are already tracked, but any new sibling would silently vanish from `git status`
# -- which is how a reference dataset gets lost without anyone noticing. The docs/ image
# and .pptx assets this also protected are gone; validation/ alone still earns the rule.
/*.hdb
/*.HDB
/*.h5
/*.hdf5
/*.stl
/*.csv
/*.json
/*.ini
/*.png
/*.pptx
/*.log

# Generated documentation. Still blanket-matched: the pandoc/pweave lane writes next
# to its sources rather than into an output directory, so there is nothing to anchor to.
**.pdf
**.html
**.docx
**.emf
**.jpg
**.jpeg
**.bin

# Packaging
ssc.deb
xdyn.deb
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.bz2

# Editors, IDEs, tooling
.cproject
.pydevproject
.metadata
.project
.settings
.vagrant
*.swp
__pycache__
.wine

# uv's default project environment. The mise tasks all set UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT into build/,
# but a bare `uv sync` in the repo root drops a venv here; pyproject.toml and uv.lock are tracked.
/.venv/

# build-host-tools.sh's output on the standalone path: protoc and grpc_cpp_plugin for this
# machine. An artifact, like the closures themselves -- under Nix it is a store path instead.
/host-tools/
